o know  the difference between a refund  and a credit a refund like i said  typically means that you've  overpaid but there are some credits that  could come back to you  and it feels like you're getting a  refund and a child tax credit  is one of those so for example last year  the child tax credit  was two thousand dollars for every child  you were claiming as a dependent  and this year it's going up to almost  thirty six hundred dollars so that's a  big difference you could see that  money back when you file in 2021  also there's a child and dependent care  tax credit  where if you are caring for children and  paying for that out of your pocket  you could be getting a tax credit for  that last year for 2020  it was 35 that you would get back up to  3 000  the big change for 2021 is now it's 50  up to 8 000 so that could also make a  big difference for families  in 2021 yeah those are some good changes  lisa thanks so much i always appreciate  your time  thanks kendall and you can get more  financial tips by visiting  lisachastain.com
 

